@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Stage 5.2 Recon iteration (Stage 10)
+
+Stage 5.2 can create a new immutable Recon run from a successful, terminal Stage 6 result. It fetches the result from the configured local Stage 6.6 endpoint; callers cannot submit result or observation content.
+
+## Endpoint
+
+```text
+POST /api/pentest/agentic-orchestrations/{orchestration_id}/reconnaissance/iterations
+```
+
+The JSON body has exactly these fields:
+
+```json
+{
+  "schema_version": "apts-stage5.2-recon-iteration-request-v1",
+  "parent_recon_run_id": "reconrun-…",
+  "action_id": "rareq-…"
+}
+```
+
+The selected action must belong to the selected parent run. Stage 5.2 reads the exact Action Request result at `/api/execution/recon-action-requests/{action_id}/results` from `APTS_STAGE6_RESULT_API_BASE` (default `http://127.0.0.1:8791`). The result must be integrity-valid, latest, terminal, successful, and bound to the same proposal, orchestration, mission, and task; its Stage 6.6 evidence must be sealed.
+
+The new run appends a bounded `RAW_EVIDENCE` observation that references the Stage 6 attempt and sealed evidence manifest. Earlier runs, requests, outputs, and evidence bundles remain unchanged. The Stage 6 result is not an authorization, vulnerability finding, or task completion signal. The iteration endpoint does not execute tools or contact targets.
+
+Repository migration 010 upgrades Stage 5.2's run store to retain multiple runs per orchestration with parent/action/result lineage. Existing runs migrate as iteration 1.
